  "title": "Jeff L NDE 5306",
  "date": "Approx. 1955",
  "content": "I was about 4 years old and had crawled underneath a desk in the living room where there was an electric outlet with several bobby pins. Using one hand, I put a pin in to one of the holes of the outlet and another pin in the other hole of the same outlet and they started moving back and forth. I then put a third pin in the outlet next to it and suddenly, I could not move. I remember all of this as clearly as if it were yesterday. Suddenly I was looking down at the room from the ceiling and could see the couch where my parents were talking, the table in front of them, the desk and the general layout of the room. My father got up and (I later realized) pulled me out from under the desk by my legs. That was the end of that memory. Strangely, I asked my parents about this decades later. They did not remember it. I did not recognize it as a NDE until after reading Raymond Moody's book ‘Life after Life’ in about 1985.",
